window.docContents[39].resolve({"/Terms/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Terms--Bound-variables___-lambdas___-quantifiers":{"contents":"\n\nCvc.lean's typed API types bound variables just like it types terms.\n\nA bound variable.\n\nIt also provides a type for collections of BVar-s.\n\nA typed-list of BVars.\n\nThe untyped API for bound variables is very similar but with no type information.\n\nCvc.Untyped.BVars is thus simply an array of untyped bound variables, and all checks are\n\nperformed at runtime. We only present the typed API in this section.\n\nAs long as this list of bound variables (and their type) is known statically, functions such as\nTerm.lambda are able to deconstruct it and infer the type of the corresponding function.\n\n\n\n\n\n","context":"Cvc.lean -- High-Level API for CVC5\u0009Terms","header":"4.4. Bound variables, lambdas, quantifiers","id":"/Terms/#Cvc___lean----High-Level-API-for-CVC5--Terms--Bound-variables___-lambdas___-quantifiers"}});